WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.410
First the New York Post reports

2
00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:05.400 line:15%
that drive-ins are thriving this year.

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.860 line:15%
Uh-huh, that's right.

4
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.610
An industry that had become just fun nostalgia

5
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.850 line:15%
is poised to continue and grow as a business,

6
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:15.520 line:15%
even as the winter months bring the cold weather.

7
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.460 line:15%
Many drive-ins are modernizing online ticketing,

8
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:22.350 line:15%
ordering concessions like hot cocoa via the app,

9
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.940 line:15%
and in car electric heaters so you can save on gas.

10
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.880 line:15%
And in a year where having a sense of community

11
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.230
has been so tough,

12
00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.423
drive-ins have been a nice rediscovery.

13
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:34.860
Yes!
(audience clapping)

14
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.670
Kicking it old school!
(audience clapping)

15
00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:37.920
Okay, next up,

16
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.870
People magazine reports that a study

17
00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.780
from the University of Rochester found out

18
00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.000
that watching TV and movies

19
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.970
can actually make your relationship stronger.

20
00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:51.920 line:15%
It's not just Netflix and chilling,

21
00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.890 line:15%
the study found that couples who engaged in conversation

22
00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:57.380 line:15%
after watching a movie or a TV show

23
00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:02.330 line:15%
saw a 50% reduction in divorce compared to a control group.

24
00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.110
It's the conversation after watching

25
00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:05.320
that keeps you together like,

26
00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:09.060
oh my gosh, Bruce Willis was dead the whole time?

27
00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.513
I love you, honey.

28
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.450
No wonder you're not fighting.

29
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:15.880
You're zoning out to the boob tube all day.

30
00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.660
Who's watching your kids, by the way?

31
00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:19.180
Oh, you don't have them?

32
00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.060
Well, you know what's also good for relationships?

33
00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.510
Anesthesia and staring at a screen

34
00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:26.270
while not communicating and bickering about daily dilemmas.

35
00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:29.440
So yeah, put on those horse blinders and a muzzle,

36
00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.179
and enjoy that relationship.

37
00:01:31.179 --> 00:01:34.870
(audience clapping)

38
00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:38.440
Here's one for all the gingers and Archies out there.

39
00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.515 line:15%
Today is national love your red hair day.

40
00:01:42.515 --> 00:01:43.770 line:15%
(audience clapping)

41
